&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Development time:&lt;/strong&gt; 4 hours &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Built with:&lt;/strong&gt; Replit, React, TypeScript, Express, and PostgreSQL&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Introduction
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Can we build a functional wellness tracking application in just four hours?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That was the challenge behind Denge, a web application that brings nutrition, activity, hydration, sleep, and weight tracking into one place.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The name Denge means “balance” in Turkish. We chose it because our project focuses on everyday habits rather than a single measurement or an unrealistic definition of a healthy lifestyle.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;During our four-hour development session, we worked on turning this idea into a working application with personal accounts, persistent records, and a multilingual interface.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This article shares what we planned to build, what we completed, the challenges we encountered, and what we would like to improve next.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The Problem We Wanted to Address
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Wellness information is often scattered across different places. Someone might record their weight in a notebook, check their steps in another application, and forget how much water they drank during the day.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Our idea was to make this information easier to organize.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Instead of building an application that promises medical advice or automatic health improvements, we focused on a practical question:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How can we help users record their daily habits and review them in one clear interface?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What We Planned to Complete
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;With only four hours available, we needed a focused scope. Our main goals were to:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create a clear dashboard showing a daily overview.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Allow users to record meals and review estimated nutritional information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support activity logging and manually entered step counts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track water intake, sleep, and weight history.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Let users set personal daily goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Add account creation and sign-in.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Save records in a database rather than keeping them only in the browser.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make the interface usable on both desktop and mobile screens.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We also wanted Denge to feel approachable. The visual direction used cream, sage, and olive colors, with simple cards and straightforward navigation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These goals gave us a concrete definition of a useful first version.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What We Completed
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;By the end of the four-hour build, we had a working version of Denge covering the main tracking features.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


1. A Daily Dashboard
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The dashboard brings the main daily information together, giving users a starting point for reviewing their records and progress toward their goals.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fdzo76rt5uj8q2nm2k2gs.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fdzo76rt5uj8q2nm2k2gs.png" alt="Denge’s dashboard displays estimated calorie intake, macronutrients, steps, water intake, and sleep duration in one daily overview." width="800" height="400"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


2. Nutrition and Meal Logging
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Users can record meals and review estimated calories and nutritional values.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We made an important distinction here: nutritional values are estimates, not precise medical measurements. Denge supports tracking and awareness; it does not prescribe a diet.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


3. Activity and Step Records
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Users can log activity and enter their daily step count.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In the current version, steps are entered manually. We have not connected the application to phone sensors, fitness watches, or other wearable devices.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


4. Water and Sleep Tracking
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The application includes records for water intake and sleep duration, allowing users to track more than food and exercise alone.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


5. Weight History and Personal Goals
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Users can record weight measurements over time and configure personal targets for calories, steps, water, sleep, and weight.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These targets are chosen by the user rather than presented as medical recommendations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Ferygbifec2kkxqgne4wn.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Ferygbifec2kkxqgne4wn.png" alt="Denge’s goals page allows users to set personal targets for daily calories, steps, water intake, sleep, and weight." width="800" height="399"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


6. Personal Accounts
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Denge includes account creation, sign-in, and an account page showing the user’s name, email address, and optional age.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We chose to collect age in years rather than a complete date of birth because the current application does not need that extra information.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


7. A Multilingual Interface
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The interface supports Turkish, Arabic, and English, including right-to-left layout support for Arabic.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This helped us consider accessibility across languages, not only across screen sizes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


How We Built It
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We developed the project using Replit, with the following stack:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Part of the Application&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Technology&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;User Interface&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;React and TypeScript&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Frontend Tooling&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Vite&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Styling&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Tailwind CSS&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Server-State Management&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;TanStack Query&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Backend API&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Node.js and Express&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Database&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;PostgreSQL&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Database Access&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Drizzle ORM&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Authentication&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Clerk&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;API Contract and Client Generation&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;OpenAPI and Orval&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The frontend communicates with the Express API, which reads and writes records in PostgreSQL.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For personal records, the backend uses the authenticated user’s identity to determine account ownership. It does not rely only on an account identifier supplied by the browser.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Using an OpenAPI contract also helped keep frontend requests and backend responses aligned.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Challenges We Encountered
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Account Creation Was More Than a Sign-Up Form
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;One issue appeared during profile completion: saving the age succeeded, but saving the name failed because the authentication configuration rejected the native name update.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We resolved this by storing Denge’s display name in the appropriate user profile metadata and updating the places where the application reads that name.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This taught us to check the entire journey—not only whether an account was created, but also whether profile information was saved, displayed correctly, and still available after refreshing the page.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Translation Required Layout Changes
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Supporting Arabic was not simply a matter of replacing Turkish or English text.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We also had to consider reading direction, alignment, longer labels, and mixed-direction content such as email addresses.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A translated interface is only useful if the layout remains comfortable to use.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


A Four-Hour Limit Required Prioritization
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The time limit encouraged us to focus on a functional core rather than attempt every possible feature.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We prioritized recording, saving, and displaying useful information. Features such as wearable integrations and advanced recommendations were outside the scope of this first version.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Completing a working prototype in four hours does not mean that every production concern is finished. Further testing and improvements remain important.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What We Want to Develop Next
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Our next priorities are:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Editable account information:&lt;/strong&gt; make it easier to update profile details.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Cross-device language preferences:&lt;/strong&gt; remember the selected language across sessions and devices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Data export and deletion:&lt;/strong&gt; give users more control over their personal records.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Further privacy testing:&lt;/strong&gt; continue checking that one account cannot access another account’s records.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Better input validation and feedback:&lt;/strong&gt; make incorrect entries easier to identify and fix.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Optional fitness integrations:&lt;/strong&gt; explore automatic activity tracking through supported services in a future version.
These are planned improvements, not features we claim are already available.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What We Learned
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The project showed us that building an application involves much more than creating attractive screens.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Authentication, database persistence, localization, and error handling all affect whether a feature works from the user’s perspective.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We also learned the value of being clear about limitations: manual step entry should be described as manual, nutritional estimates should be labeled as estimates, and planned features should be separated from completed ones.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Conclusion
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In four hours, we built a functional first version of Denge that combines several daily wellness records in one application.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The result gives us a foundation to continue developing, while the experience helped us understand the importance of realistic scope, complete user journeys, and clear communication.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Denge is not a replacement for professional medical or nutritional advice. Its purpose is to help users organize their records and become more aware of their everyday habits.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Created by &lt;strong&gt;Joud Kattaa Shikhoni&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;Jana Sweity&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Source Code
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/joudkattaa/Saglikli-YasamDa-Xiao-Gui-Lu" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Explore Denge on GitHub&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Building Denge in four hours was a valuable lesson in prioritizing features, making technical decisions, and creating a multilingual user experience.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What would you improve or add to Denge next?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


TL;DR
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The shadcn CLI has no merge: add --diff lists every difference between your copy and the registry without saying which side made it, and add --overwrite replaces the file, edits included. To keep your edits, run a 3-way merge on each file (the copy as installed, your copy and the new upstream) with git merge-file, keeping the installed copies on a git branch. The Wingo UI CLI saves the installed copy itself, so npx wingo-ui@latest update runs that merge and stops only where both sides changed the same or adjacent lines.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You installed a shadcn/ui button a few months ago, gave it a brand variant and a taller default size, and now upstream has changes you want. When you try to update shadcn components that you have edited, the CLI gives you two tools: &lt;code&gt;add --overwrite&lt;/code&gt;, which replaces the file and your edits with it, and &lt;code&gt;add --diff&lt;/code&gt;, which lists every difference between your copy and the registry without saying who made each one. This tutorial covers why copies drift, what shadcn diff can and cannot tell you, and how a 3-way merge pulls upstream fixes into files you already changed: first with a git script for stock shadcn/ui, then with a CLI that does it for you.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Why do copied components drift from upstream?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Because the copy stops changing the moment the CLI writes it, and upstream keeps going. A shadcn component is a file in your repo with no version attached. As of October 2026 (shadcn 4.21.4), &lt;code&gt;components.json&lt;/code&gt; stores settings such as your style, Tailwind, aliases, icon library and registries, and nothing about which components you installed or when. Meanwhile upstream ships changes like these:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;September 2026:&lt;/strong&gt; "Every shadcn component now imports &lt;code&gt;cn&lt;/code&gt; from the &lt;code&gt;cn&lt;/code&gt; package" (&lt;a href="https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/changelog" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;shadcn changelog&lt;/a&gt;). The import line changed in every component.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;March 2025:&lt;/strong&gt; new dark mode colors. The &lt;a href="https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/tailwind-v4" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Tailwind v4 page&lt;/a&gt; tells existing projects to run &lt;code&gt;add --all --overwrite&lt;/code&gt;, then "Review and re-apply any changes you made to your components."&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Bug fixes&lt;/strong&gt;, which land the same way. The Wingo UI &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/data-table" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Data Table&lt;/a&gt; 1.0.1 fixed header cells that dropped over the first row while the header was pinned. The fix was one &lt;code&gt;className&lt;/code&gt; in a file of almost 4,000 lines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What does shadcn diff show, and what does it miss?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It shows a 2-way diff: your file against the registry's current version, after the CLI applies your aliases and icon library. The standalone command is deprecated; in shadcn 4.21.4 its help reads "[DEPRECATED] Use &lt;code&gt;add [component] --diff&lt;/code&gt; instead." The flag arrived with &lt;a href="https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/changelog/2026-03-cli-v4" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;shadcn CLI v4&lt;/a&gt; in March 2026, together with &lt;code&gt;--dry-run&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;--view&lt;/code&gt;, and without a path it shows the first 5 files.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We tested it in a scratch Next.js project: the shadcn button as published in March 2026, plus two local edits, a &lt;code&gt;brand&lt;/code&gt; variant and a 40px default size. This is the trimmed output of &lt;code&gt;npx shadcn@4.21.4 add button --diff&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight diff"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;@@ -1,9 +1,8 @@&lt;/span&gt;
import * as React from "react"
import { cva, type VariantProps } from "class-variance-authority"
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+import { cn } from "cn"
&lt;/span&gt; import { Slot } from "radix-ui"
&lt;span class="err"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="gd"&gt;-import { cn } from "@/lib/utils"
-
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;@@ -19,10 +18,9 @@&lt;/span&gt;
link: "text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline",
&lt;span class="gd"&gt;-        brand: "bg-orange-600 text-white hover:bg-orange-600/90",
&lt;/span&gt;       },
size: {
&lt;span class="gd"&gt;-        default: "h-10 px-4 py-2 has-[&amp;gt;svg]:px-3",
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+        default: "h-9 px-4 py-2 has-[&amp;gt;svg]:px-3",
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The first hunk is upstream's change. The other two are our edits, shown as lines &lt;code&gt;--overwrite&lt;/code&gt; would undo. Nothing in the output tells them apart, because a 2-way diff only knows two files. To know which side changed a line, you need a third: the component as it was installed, which shadcn does not keep. In the same project, the deprecated &lt;code&gt;npx shadcn@4.21.4 diff button&lt;/code&gt; printed "No updates found for button.", so stick with the flag.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For edited files, shadcn points you to your coding agent. The CLI v4 post suggests asking it to "check for updates from @shadcn and merge with my local changes", and the &lt;a href="https://github.com/shadcn-ui/ui/blob/main/skills/shadcn/SKILL.md" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;official skill&lt;/a&gt; tells the agent to "read the local file, analyze the diff, and apply upstream updates while preserving local modifications." The agent sees the same 2-way diff, so unless it digs the installed copy out of git history, it has to guess which side made each change. The script below gets that copy from git, for you or for the agent.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


How do you update all shadcn components at once?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Re-add them with &lt;code&gt;--overwrite&lt;/code&gt;, which is safe only for files you never edited. shadcn 4.21.4 has no &lt;code&gt;update&lt;/code&gt; command, so "shadcn update all components" comes down to &lt;code&gt;npx shadcn@latest add --all --overwrite&lt;/code&gt;. It re-adds every component in the registry, including ones you never installed, and replaces your files. Re-running &lt;code&gt;init --reinstall&lt;/code&gt; first offers to overwrite &lt;code&gt;components.json&lt;/code&gt;, then reinstalls the components you already have, with a warning that they "will be re-installed and overwritten". Find the files you never touched first:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;for &lt;/span&gt;f &lt;span class="k"&gt;in &lt;/span&gt;components/ui/&lt;span class="k"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;.tsx&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;do
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;first&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;$(&lt;/span&gt;git log &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--diff-filter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;A &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--format&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;%H &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;$f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; | &lt;span class="nb"&gt;tail&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
git diff &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--quiet&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;$first&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;$f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;echo&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"untouched: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;$f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;done&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;A file that still matches the commit that added it is safe to overwrite, so pass only those names to &lt;code&gt;npx shadcn@latest add &amp;lt;name...&amp;gt; --overwrite&lt;/code&gt;. Merge the rest.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


How do you update shadcn components you have edited?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Merge three versions of each file: the copy the CLI installed (the base), your copy, and the new upstream. Where only one side changed a region, the merge takes that side; where both changed the same lines, it writes conflict markers. This is the step shadcn's own docs skip when you upgrade shadcn components: they stop at re-applying your changes by hand or asking an agent. &lt;code&gt;git merge-file&lt;/code&gt; does the merge; the work is getting the base and the upstream into files, and a branch that holds only pristine CLI output does both.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


1. Create a branch with the files as installed
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Run this once. It rebuilds each component from the commit that first added it, which is the copy the CLI wrote if you committed before editing:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;git switch &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-c&lt;/span&gt; shadcn-upstream
&lt;span class="k"&gt;for &lt;/span&gt;f &lt;span class="k"&gt;in &lt;/span&gt;components/ui/&lt;span class="k"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;.tsx&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;do
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;first&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;$(&lt;/span&gt;git log &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--diff-filter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;A &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--format&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;%H &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;$f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; | &lt;span class="nb"&gt;tail&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
git show &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;$first&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;$f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;$f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;done
&lt;/span&gt;git commit &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-am&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"shadcn: components as installed"&lt;/span&gt;
git switch -
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


2. Write the new upstream on that branch and merge it
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Run this for every update. List the components you have, since &lt;code&gt;--all&lt;/code&gt; would also install the ones you don't:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;git switch shadcn-upstream
npx shadcn@latest add button dialog &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--overwrite&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--yes&lt;/span&gt;
git add &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-A&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; git commit &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-m&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"shadcn: upstream &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;$(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;date&lt;/span&gt; +%F&lt;span class="si"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
git switch -

&lt;span class="k"&gt;for &lt;/span&gt;f &lt;span class="k"&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="si"&gt;$(&lt;/span&gt;git diff &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--name-only&lt;/span&gt; shadcn-upstream~1 shadcn-upstream &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--&lt;/span&gt; components/ui&lt;span class="si"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;do&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c"&gt;# a file upstream added: take it as is&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-f&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;$f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;then &lt;/span&gt;git show &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"shadcn-upstream:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;$f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;$f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;continue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;fi
&lt;/span&gt;git show &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"shadcn-upstream~1:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;$f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; /tmp/base.tsx
git show &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"shadcn-upstream:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;$f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; /tmp/upstream.tsx
git merge-file &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-L&lt;/span&gt; yours &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-L&lt;/span&gt; installed &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-L&lt;/span&gt; upstream &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;$f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; /tmp/base.tsx /tmp/upstream.tsx &lt;span class="se"&gt;\&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;echo&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"resolve conflicts in &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;$f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;done&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;git merge-file&lt;/code&gt; writes the result into your file and exits with the number of conflicts, so the loop names every file that needs a look. If the commit on the upstream branch reports nothing to commit, upstream has not changed and there is nothing to merge. Otherwise the branch now holds the upstream you just merged, so the next update uses it as the base.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If your components import hooks (the sidebar's &lt;code&gt;use-mobile.ts&lt;/code&gt;), add &lt;code&gt;hooks/*.ts&lt;/code&gt; to the step 1 loop and &lt;code&gt;hooks&lt;/code&gt; to the &lt;code&gt;git diff&lt;/code&gt; in step 2. And when you add a component later, run the same &lt;code&gt;add&lt;/code&gt; on the &lt;code&gt;shadcn-upstream&lt;/code&gt; branch and commit it there too; without that, the loop finds no base for the file and every line that differs from upstream becomes a conflict.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


3. Check what changed outside the components
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The loop only touches &lt;code&gt;components/ui&lt;/code&gt;. On the upstream branch the CLI may also have added npm packages and CSS variables:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;git diff shadcn-upstream~1 shadcn-upstream &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--&lt;/span&gt; package.json app/globals.css
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


What happened when we ran it
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We ran the script with shadcn 4.21.4 on the scratch project above. Both edits stayed, the button picked up &lt;code&gt;import { cn } from "cn"&lt;/code&gt;, and the untouched dialog was replaced. Step 3 showed &lt;code&gt;"cn": "^0.4.0"&lt;/code&gt; added to &lt;code&gt;package.json&lt;/code&gt;; until &lt;code&gt;cn&lt;/code&gt; is in your branch's &lt;code&gt;package.json&lt;/code&gt;, the merged button fails on a clean install. For that particular change, also run &lt;code&gt;npx shadcn@latest migrate cn&lt;/code&gt;. In a test project it installed &lt;code&gt;cn&lt;/code&gt; and turned &lt;code&gt;lib/utils.ts&lt;/code&gt; into &lt;code&gt;export { cn } from "cn"&lt;/code&gt;, so every &lt;code&gt;@/lib/utils&lt;/code&gt; import in your own code keeps working.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Two caveats. If you edited a component before its first commit, step 1 records your edit as the installed copy, and the first merge silently reverts it, so read &lt;code&gt;git diff&lt;/code&gt; after every merge. And if a formatter rewrote a component, run it on the base and upstream files too before merging. On a Prettier-reformatted copy of the Data Table, the merge stopped with one conflict exactly where upstream had changed the file; with all three files formatted the same way, it merged clean.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Can a CLI run the 3-way merge for you?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Yes, if it keeps the base itself. When &lt;code&gt;npx wingo-ui@latest add&lt;/code&gt; installs a component, it records the version and a hash per file in &lt;code&gt;wingo-ui.json&lt;/code&gt; and saves the pristine copy under &lt;code&gt;.wingo-ui/base/&lt;/code&gt;. Commit both. From then on, as of CLI 1.0.3:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;npx wingo-ui@latest outdated               &lt;span class="c"&gt;# installed vs latest, the bump, local edits&lt;/span&gt;
npx wingo-ui@latest diff data-table &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--base&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c"&gt;# only your edits since install&lt;/span&gt;
npx wingo-ui@latest update &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--dry-run&lt;/span&gt;       &lt;span class="c"&gt;# what would merge, nothing written&lt;/span&gt;
npx wingo-ui@latest update                 &lt;span class="c"&gt;# 3-way merge into every installed item&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;For each file, &lt;code&gt;update&lt;/code&gt; compares your copy, the base and the new release. An untouched file is replaced. An edited file gets the upstream changes merged in, and its base moves to the new version for next time. It prints the release notes of every version you skipped, installs new dependencies, and reports files a release no longer ships without deleting them.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We replayed the real Data Table 1.0.1 fix through the CLI's merge code, with &lt;code&gt;defaultPageSize&lt;/code&gt; changed from 25 to 50 in our copy. The merge was clean: the fix landed and the 50 stayed. Then we also added &lt;code&gt;select-none&lt;/code&gt; to the header cell's classes, on the exact line the fix rewrote, and got one conflict:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;local&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;cn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;group/head relative select-none&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;reorder&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;cursor-grab active:cursor-grabbing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;isDragging&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;opacity-40&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;=======&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;cn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// a sticky header cell is already a containing block; a plain "relative" would win over "sticky" in cn and&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// leave the sticky top offset on a relative cell, pushing the header down over the first row&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;group/head [&amp;amp;:not(.sticky)]:relative&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;reorder&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;cursor-grab active:cursor-grabbing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;isDragging&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;opacity-40&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;wingo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ui&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mf"&gt;1.0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Keep upstream's block, add &lt;code&gt;select-none&lt;/code&gt; to its first string, delete the markers. Or settle every conflict at once with &lt;code&gt;update --theirs&lt;/code&gt; (take the release) or &lt;code&gt;--ours&lt;/code&gt; (keep yours); both also clear markers an earlier run left behind. &lt;code&gt;git merge-file&lt;/code&gt; produced the same merge in both cases, apart from the marker label. In both tools an edit on the line right next to an upstream change also conflicts, while one untouched line between them was enough for a clean merge.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The table below has &lt;code&gt;maxHeight&lt;/code&gt; set, so it scrolls inside its own box, which is the case the fix repaired.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Live demo: Data Table.&lt;/strong&gt; The original article embeds an interactive demo here (Scroll inside the table: the header row stays pinned at the top of the box while the rows move under it. Below 768px the rows turn into cards). &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/blog/update-shadcn-components-without-losing-edits" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Try it live on wingo-ui.com&lt;/a&gt; or open the &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/data-table" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Data Table docs&lt;/a&gt;. Install: &lt;code&gt;npx wingo-ui@latest add data-table&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We also ran the published CLI end to end on the free &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/field" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Field&lt;/a&gt;, whose 1.0.1 fix keeps focus in an input when its error clears, after changing its &lt;code&gt;optionalLabel&lt;/code&gt; default. &lt;code&gt;update&lt;/code&gt; printed &lt;code&gt;merged components/ui/field.tsx&lt;/code&gt; with the release note, and the edit stayed. Two guard rails: without a base copy (say &lt;code&gt;.wingo-ui/&lt;/code&gt; was never committed and a teammate runs the update) the CLI does not guess and asks for &lt;code&gt;--theirs&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;--ours&lt;/code&gt;, and while conflicts remain it exits with code 1, so a CI step fails instead of shipping markers. Agents can run the same version check through the &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/docs/mcp" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;MCP server&lt;/a&gt;'s &lt;code&gt;check_updates&lt;/code&gt; tool, which compares &lt;code&gt;wingo-ui.json&lt;/code&gt; with the latest release and lists the release notes. The full reference is in the &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/docs/updates" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;updates docs&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


How do you keep the next update conflict-free?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Own fewer lines of each component. Conflicts only happen where you and upstream change the same or adjacent lines.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Set defaults from outside.&lt;/strong&gt; Every Wingo UI component reads app-wide defaults through &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/ui-config" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;UIProvider&lt;/a&gt;, so a radius, a page size or the phone layout of a dialog needs no edit to the file. Explicit props win, then the provider, then the component's own defaults.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Wrap for behavior.&lt;/strong&gt; A &lt;code&gt;SubmitButton&lt;/code&gt; that composes the &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/button" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Button&lt;/a&gt; lives in your code and never conflicts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Keep your formatter off copied files.&lt;/strong&gt; Add &lt;code&gt;components/ui&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code&gt;.prettierignore&lt;/code&gt;, or each upstream change near a reformatted line turns into a conflict.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Update a release or two at a time&lt;/strong&gt;, so each merge stays small enough to review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The 25 to 50 page size from the test above, a pill-shaped button and a &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/dialog" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Dialog&lt;/a&gt; that stays a centered card on phones, all without touching a component file:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/providers.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;use client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ReactNode&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;UIProvider&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@/lib/ui-config&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;Providers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ReactNode&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;UIProvider&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;defaults&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;radius&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;full&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;dialog&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;responsive&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;data-table&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;defaultPageSize&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;50&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;UIProvider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Wrap &lt;code&gt;{children}&lt;/code&gt; in &lt;code&gt;app/layout.tsx&lt;/code&gt; with &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;Providers&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, and every Button, Dialog and Data Table under it starts from these defaults. The demo shows the same mechanism on two buttons:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Live demo: UIProvider.&lt;/strong&gt; The original article embeds an interactive demo here (The first button uses its built-in defaults; the two below get radius full, size lg and tone brand from a UIProvider, and the outline one keeps the variant it passes itself). &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/blog/update-shadcn-components-without-losing-edits" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Try it live on wingo-ui.com&lt;/a&gt; or open the &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/ui-config" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;UIProvider docs&lt;/a&gt;. Install: &lt;code&gt;npx wingo-ui@latest add ui-config&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For one component at a time, see the &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/blog/category/components" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;component guides&lt;/a&gt;, starting with the &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/blog/react-form-components-guide" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React form components guide&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What should you do next?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On stock shadcn/ui, create the &lt;code&gt;shadcn-upstream&lt;/code&gt; branch now, while your history still shows what the CLI wrote. If you want the merge built in, install the free Button and Dialog with &lt;code&gt;npx wingo-ui@latest add button dialog&lt;/code&gt;, commit &lt;code&gt;wingo-ui.json&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;.wingo-ui/&lt;/code&gt;, and run &lt;code&gt;npx wingo-ui@latest update --dry-run&lt;/code&gt; after the next release. The Data Table is part of &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/pricing" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Wingo UI Pro&lt;/a&gt;. The &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/blog/shadcn-alternatives" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;shadcn alternatives&lt;/a&gt; post compares how other libraries handle updates.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Components in this post
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/button" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Button&lt;/a&gt; (Free): The button every screen starts with: five variants, six tones, three sizes plus icon sizes, and a loading state that never jumps. Install: &lt;code&gt;npx wingo-ui@latest add button&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/dialog" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Dialog&lt;/a&gt; (Free): The modal for focused tasks: a spring-scaled card on desktop that becomes a bottom sheet on phones, with nesting and a scrolling body. Install: &lt;code&gt;npx wingo-ui@latest add dialog&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/data-table" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Data Table&lt;/a&gt; (Pro): The admin table on TanStack Table v9: search, filters, sorting, bulk actions, pinning, resizing, virtualization and cards on phones. Install: &lt;code&gt;npx wingo-ui@latest add data-table&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/field" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Field&lt;/a&gt; (Free): The wrapper every form control shares: label, hint, animated error and counter, fieldsets, and the one box recipe all inputs use. Install: &lt;code&gt;npx wingo-ui@latest add field&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/ui-config" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;UIProvider&lt;/a&gt; (Free): App-wide configuration for Wingo UI: default props for every component, the Intl locale and the reduced-motion policy. Install: &lt;code&gt;npx wingo-ui@latest add ui-config&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


FAQ
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


How do you update shadcn components?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Run npx shadcn@latest add &amp;lt;name&amp;gt; --diff to see how your file differs from the registry, then npx shadcn@latest add &amp;lt;name&amp;gt; --overwrite to replace it. Overwrite drops your edits, so for files you changed, merge three versions (as installed, yours and upstream) with git merge-file instead.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Is the shadcn diff command deprecated?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Yes. As of shadcn 4.21.4 (October 2026) its help text says to use add &amp;lt;component&amp;gt; --diff instead. The flag arrived with shadcn CLI v4 in March 2026, along with --dry-run and --view.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


How do I update all shadcn components at once?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;npx shadcn@latest add --all --overwrite re-adds every component in the registry and replaces your files, edits included. Overwrite only the files that still match the commit that added them, and merge the ones you changed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Why does a 3-way merge keep my edits when a diff cannot?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A diff compares two files, so your edits and upstream's changes look the same. A 3-way merge also reads the file as it was installed, so it knows which side changed each line and only stops where both sides changed the same or adjacent lines.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Can the Wingo UI CLI update components I installed with shadcn?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;No. wingo-ui update only merges items it installed itself, because it needs the base copy it saved in .wingo-ui/base at install time. For stock shadcn/ui files, use the git merge-file script from this post.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This article was originally published on the Wingo UI blog: &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/blog/update-shadcn-components-without-losing-edits" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;How to Update shadcn Components Without Losing Edits&lt;/a&gt;. The original has the live, interactive demos and is kept up to date.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I'm officially &lt;strong&gt;Microsoft Certified: Azure Fundamentals&lt;/strong&gt;! ☁️&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I'm a self-taught developer focused on backend engineering. I took the AZ-900 exam to understand the cloud platform behind so many modern systems: compute, networking, storage, identity, security, and how cloud services are priced and governed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To prepare, I joined the &lt;strong&gt;Power Learn Project Vibe Coding Hackathon (AZ-900 Exam Prep Edition)&lt;/strong&gt; and used it to build something I could study with.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What I built
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Smart Quiz Builder&lt;/strong&gt; is an unofficial AZ-900 practice app. You answer exam-style questions and get an explanation for each answer, so you learn why an answer is right or wrong instead of memorising it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;🔗 &lt;strong&gt;Live demo:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://az900-smart-quiz.vercel.app" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://az900-smart-quiz.vercel.app&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
💻 &lt;strong&gt;Code:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://github.com/cyn4sh/az900-smart-quiz" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://github.com/cyn4sh/az900-smart-quiz&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The stack
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;React + TypeScript (Vite):&lt;/strong&gt; the quiz flow, results screen and history view.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Supabase:&lt;/strong&gt; anonymous auth, so anyone can use the app without signing up, plus storage for quiz attempts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Vercel:&lt;/strong&gt; deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Cursor:&lt;/strong&gt; my AI coding tool for the hackathon.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


How I approached it
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Questions live in a typed file, not the database.&lt;/strong&gt; The question set sits in a typed TypeScript file, and Supabase only stores attempts. That keeps the data model simple and the questions easy to review and edit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;I reviewed everything the AI generated.&lt;/strong&gt; I built the app in chunks with Cursor and checked each chunk before moving on, making sure the build and lint passed. Vibe coding is fast, but you still own the code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;I designed before I built.&lt;/strong&gt; I settled the look and architecture before opening the editor: a calm dark "late-night study" theme, mobile-first, with a teal accent for correct answers and coral for wrong ones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What I learned
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Building a study tool while studying for the exam made the concepts stick. Writing questions and explanations forced me to understand each topic well enough to explain it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What's next
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;AZ-900 is a fundamentals cert, so I see it as a foundation, not a finish line. Next, I'm going deeper into backend development and infrastructure, building projects that put these cloud concepts into practice.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Credential
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Verify my certification here: &lt;a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/api/credentials/share/en-gb/Ashfall-1799/BEC3B0858B5CEEA1?sharingId=CAF4767643DF5F26" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://learn.microsoft.com/api/credentials/share/en-gb/Ashfall-1799/BEC3B0858B5CEEA1?sharingId=CAF4767643DF5F26&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you're preparing for AZ-900, try the quiz app and tell me what you think. 🙌&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Most people who bounce off a web3 app never get past the "install a browser extension and write down 24 words" step. An embedded wallet removes that step: the user signs in with Google, gets an address, and can send a transaction without ever holding gas.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This post walks through wiring that up in a React app with &lt;a href="https://docs.cavos.xyz" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;code&gt;@cavos/kit&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, an embedded wallet SDK that supports Starknet, Solana and Stellar. I'll use Starknet for the main example because it shows the most moving parts (a paymaster, a multicall, lazy deployment), and point out where Solana and Stellar differ.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;By the end you'll have:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;a provider that wraps your app&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;a sign-in button with Google login&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;a gasless transaction from a wallet that didn't exist on-chain a minute earlier&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;a recovery path so users don't lose access when they switch phones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What actually happens under the hood
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It helps to have the model in your head before writing code, because it explains the API.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Authentication only identifies the user.&lt;/strong&gt; Google (or Apple, or an email code) produces a stable &lt;code&gt;userId&lt;/code&gt;. The login never signs transactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Connect derives an address.&lt;/strong&gt; The kit looks up &lt;code&gt;(userId, appId, chain)&lt;/code&gt; in the Cavos registry. If there's an entry, you get that address back. If not, this device computes one and claims it. Connect &lt;strong&gt;never deploys&lt;/strong&gt; anything.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The first &lt;code&gt;execute&lt;/code&gt; deploys.&lt;/strong&gt; On an undeployed account, the first transaction deploys the account and runs your operation atomically, in one sponsored transaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On Starknet, the account is the standard, upgradeable OpenZeppelin &lt;code&gt;AccountUpgradeable&lt;/code&gt; (v3.0.0), i.e. an audited OpenZeppelin account contract, not a custom one. Its stark key is derived from a per-user MasterDEK that lives on the user's devices. There's no on-chain device list: a new device restores the MasterDEK off-chain, via a passkey or the recovery enclave, and derives the same key.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


1. Install and get your keys
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;npm &lt;span class="nb"&gt;install&lt;/span&gt; @cavos/kit
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The React bindings ship in the same package under &lt;code&gt;@cavos/kit/react&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Create an app in the Cavos dashboard and copy its App ID. For Starknet you also need a paymaster API key.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c"&gt;# .env.local&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nv"&gt;NEXT_PUBLIC_CAVOS_APP_ID&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;your-app-id
&lt;span class="nv"&gt;NEXT_PUBLIC_CAVOS_PAYMASTER_API_KEY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;your-paymaster-key
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;A note on that paymaster key: it ends up in browser code, so treat it as a client-visible, app-scoped sponsorship credential, not a secret. Before going to production, limit it by app, environment, origin, rate and spend in the sponsorship service.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;While you're in the dashboard, register your OAuth callback URLs under &lt;strong&gt;Dashboard → App → Callback URLs&lt;/strong&gt;. They're matched exactly (scheme, host, path, no trailing slash, no wildcards), so add &lt;code&gt;http://localhost:3000&lt;/code&gt; and any preview or tunnel domains you use. Google login will reject a redirect URI that isn't on the list, and this is the most common "why doesn't login work" moment.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


2. Wrap your app in &lt;code&gt;CavosProvider&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/providers.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;use client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;CavosProvider&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@cavos/kit/react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;Providers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ReactNode&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CavosProvider&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;config&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;appId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;process&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;NEXT_PUBLIC_CAVOS_APP_ID&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;chains&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;starknet&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;defaultChain&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;starknet&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;network&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;testnet&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Starknet Sepolia&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;appSalt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;my-app&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;paymasterApiKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;process&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;NEXT_PUBLIC_CAVOS_PAYMASTER_API_KEY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;socialRecovery&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;deviceApproval&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;enclave&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;modal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;appName&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;My App&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;light&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;providers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;google&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;email&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CavosProvider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;A few of these fields deserve a sentence each:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;appSalt&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; goes into the key derivation. Pick it once and never change it. A changed salt derives a different key and address, which silently moves every existing user to a new, empty wallet. In development the provider warns you if the salt changed since the browser last connected, and you can run the same checks yourself with &lt;code&gt;validateCavosConfig(config)&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;paymasterApiKey&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; only belongs here when &lt;code&gt;"starknet"&lt;/code&gt; is in &lt;code&gt;chains&lt;/code&gt;. Putting it on a config that doesn't use Starknet is reported as a config error in development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;socialRecovery: true&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; turns on hardware-isolated recovery: the enclave wraps the MasterDEK so a user who signs in again on a new device can get their wallet back. It needs &lt;code&gt;appId&lt;/code&gt;, and the feature also has to be enabled for the app's environment in the dashboard. More on that below.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;deviceApproval&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; is &lt;code&gt;"enclave"&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;"passkey"&lt;/code&gt;. It already defaults to &lt;code&gt;"enclave"&lt;/code&gt; when &lt;code&gt;socialRecovery&lt;/code&gt; is on, so the line above is explicit rather than required. &lt;code&gt;"passkey"&lt;/code&gt; only works with a single chain; the provider throws if you combine it with several.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;modal&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; mounts the built-in login modal. Omit it if you want to build your own UI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you're on Next.js App Router, render &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;Providers&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; in your root layout.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


3. Add a sign-in button
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;useCavos()&lt;/code&gt; is the main hook. It gives you state and actions from anywhere under the provider.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;use client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useCavos&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@cavos/kit/react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;WalletButton&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;address&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;isAuthenticated&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;isLoading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;walletStatus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;openModal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;logout&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useCavos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;isLoading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Connecting…&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;isAuthenticated&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;openModal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Sign in&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;address&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;walletStatus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;isUndeployed&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Not deployed yet&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Deployed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;logout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Sign out&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;openModal()&lt;/code&gt; opens the hosted flow with the providers you listed. If you'd rather skip the modal and put a "Continue with Google" button directly in your own UI, call &lt;code&gt;login&lt;/code&gt; instead:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;login&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useCavos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;login&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;google&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Continue with Google&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;login("google")&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;login("apple")&lt;/code&gt; start OAuth. For email there's &lt;code&gt;sendOtp(email)&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;verifyOtp(email, code)&lt;/code&gt;. One caveat from the docs: with the enclave setup (&lt;code&gt;deviceApproval: "enclave"&lt;/code&gt;), the modal uses a magic link for email, because an email OTP doesn't yield a token the recovery enclave accepts.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


The OAuth return trip
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You don't need a separate callback page or any extra code for the Google redirect. When the browser comes back, the URL carries a short-lived one-time code (&lt;code&gt;?cavos_auth_code=…&lt;/code&gt;). &lt;code&gt;CavosProvider&lt;/code&gt; checks for it on mount, strips it from the address bar right away, and exchanges it for an identity before connecting the wallet. While that runs, &lt;code&gt;isLoading&lt;/code&gt; is true and the modal shows its "connecting" state; if it fails, the message lands in &lt;code&gt;authError&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Two things are on you:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The provider has to be mounted on the page Google redirects back to. That's automatic if it lives in your root layout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;That URL has to be registered in the dashboard (see step 1).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you build your own login flow outside the provider, &lt;code&gt;useCavos()&lt;/code&gt; also exposes &lt;code&gt;handleCallback(authData, redirectUri?)&lt;/code&gt; for handling the code yourself, but with the provider in place you shouldn't need it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;logout()&lt;/code&gt; clears the persisted identity and session token. It doesn't sign the user out of Google, and the stored keys stay on the device, so the next login is silent.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Already have auth?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you use Clerk, Auth0 or your own sessions, pass the signed-in user to the provider through the &lt;code&gt;identity&lt;/code&gt; prop instead. Cavos login turns off: the modal isn't mounted and &lt;code&gt;login()&lt;/code&gt; throws. Pass &lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt; while your auth loads or after sign-out, and use an immutable primary key as &lt;code&gt;userId&lt;/code&gt;, not an email that can change. A different &lt;code&gt;userId&lt;/code&gt; means a different wallet. The authentication section of the docs covers this setup.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


4. Send a gasless transaction
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On Starknet, the context's &lt;code&gt;execute(calls)&lt;/code&gt; sends a multicall signed by the stark key. It's sponsored by default and returns &lt;code&gt;{ transactionHash }&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;use client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useCavos&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@cavos/kit/react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;TOKEN&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;0x...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ERC-20 contract address&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;SendButton&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;to&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;to&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;execute&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;walletStatus&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useCavos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;hash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setHash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setError&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;send&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setError&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;try&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// u256 amounts are two felts: low, high&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;transactionHash&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;execute&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;([&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;contractAddress&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;TOKEN&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;entrypoint&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;transfer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;calldata&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;to&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;1000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setHash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;transactionHash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;catch &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setError&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;instanceof&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Error&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;walletStatus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;needsDeviceApproval&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;This device needs to be restored before it can sign.&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;send&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Send&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;hash&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Tx: &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;hash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The important bit is which states can execute:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Status&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Meaning&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Can execute?&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;undeployed&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Address derived, no on-chain account yet&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Yes, first execute deploys and runs atomically&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;ready&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;This device holds the account key&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Yes&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;needs-device-approval&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The wallet exists, but this device holds no key&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;No, restore first&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So you don't need a separate "deploy wallet" step or button. A brand-new user can sign in and send their first transaction in the same session, and the paymaster covers both the deployment and the call.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For amounts, convert human input to base units by multiplying by &lt;code&gt;10 ** decimals&lt;/code&gt;. The docs list the decimals per chain as Solana 9, Stellar 7, and 18 for the Starknet fee token.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Solana and Stellar
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The context's &lt;code&gt;execute&lt;/code&gt; is Starknet-only. For Solana and Stellar, narrow on &lt;code&gt;wallet.chain&lt;/code&gt; and call the wallet directly:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;wallet&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useCavos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;wallet&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;chain&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;solana&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;signature&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;wallet&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;execute&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;_000_000n&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;recipient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// lamports&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;else&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;wallet&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;chain&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;stellar&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;hash&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;wallet&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;execute&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;_000_000n&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;recipient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// stroops&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;On Solana the hosted relayer becomes the fee payer (arbitrary programs are allowlisted per app), and on Stellar it can sponsor reserves and fee-bump submission. Neither needs a paymaster key. If you configure several chains, &lt;code&gt;setChain("stellar")&lt;/code&gt; switches the active wallet without re-authenticating.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


5. Don't skip recovery
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is the part people leave for later and regret. The keys live on the user's devices and never leave them. If a user loses every device and nothing was set up, &lt;strong&gt;Cavos can't restore access&lt;/strong&gt;, because no Cavos key can move the funds. So the way back has to exist before it's needed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On Starknet (and Solana and native Stellar), recovery means getting the MasterDEK onto a new device, off-chain. There are two paths:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The enclave.&lt;/strong&gt; With &lt;code&gt;socialRecovery: true&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;deviceApproval: "enclave"&lt;/code&gt; (the config above), the provider enrolls after a fresh login and unwraps on a device that doesn't have the key. The user just signs in with Google again.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;A passkey.&lt;/strong&gt; Offer it after sign-up, never during OAuth. Sign-up doesn't prompt for one by default.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;walletStatus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;passkeySupported&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;enrollPasskeyDefault&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useCavos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;passkeySupported&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;walletStatus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;hasPasskey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;enrollPasskeyDefault&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// one platform prompt (Face ID / Touch ID / PIN)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;On a fresh device where the automatic path didn't run (for example, the user dismissed the prompt), &lt;code&gt;walletStatus.needsDeviceApproval&lt;/code&gt; is true and you can restore from the passkey:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;walletStatus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;approveDeviceWithPasskey&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useCavos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;walletStatus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;needsDeviceApproval&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;approveDeviceWithPasskey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// restores the MasterDEK; not an on-chain approval&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;To decide whether to nudge a user, read &lt;code&gt;walletStatus.recovery&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;walletStatus&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useCavos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;walletStatus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;isReady&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;walletStatus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;recovery&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;protected&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// show: "Add a passkey so you can sign in on a new device."&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;recovery.protected&lt;/code&gt; starts &lt;code&gt;false&lt;/code&gt; and flips once its lookup returns, so treat it as "not known to be protected" for the first moments of a connect. Don't flash a scary warning on the first render.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Checklist before production
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;appSalt&lt;/code&gt; is final and committed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Every production and preview callback URL is registered in the dashboard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The paymaster key is scoped and limited by origin, rate and spend.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;network&lt;/code&gt; is switched from &lt;code&gt;"testnet"&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code&gt;"mainnet"&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Users are prompted to set up recovery once they're signed in.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Wrapping up
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The whole integration is a provider, one hook, and a decision about recovery. Users sign in with an account they already have, the first transaction deploys their wallet without them noticing, and nobody needs to buy gas to try your app.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you want to go further:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The &lt;a href="https://docs.cavos.xyz" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Cavos docs&lt;/a&gt; cover per-chain configuration, signing messages and signing without submitting, and React Native.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://cavos.xyz/blog/how-to-add-an-embedded-wallet" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;How to add an embedded wallet&lt;/a&gt; is a longer guide that also covers the registry model and the "bring your own auth" setup.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The &lt;a href="https://cavos.xyz/embedded-wallet" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;embedded wallet&lt;/a&gt; page has the product overview across Starknet, Solana and Stellar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Hi everyone, &lt;a href="https://x.com/sebastienlorber" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Seb&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://x.com/jaworek3211" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Jan&lt;/a&gt; here 👋!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It’s a heavy security week, with patches from React and Next.js. Not React-related, but there's also a very bad “php2shell” vulnerability that has just been disclosed. Upgrade now!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On mobile, React Native 0.88 is out, switching to the web event model with no breaking changes. Expo SDK 58 ships with tons of features, ready for iOS 27 and iPhone Duo.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Outside React, TypeScript makes the headlines. v7.1 is in beta, with a new API to build devtools upon. A Rust port of the type checker is now backed by Cloudflare/VoidZero, and already faster than the official Go version.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Let's dive in!&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;💡 Subscribe to the official newsletter to receive an email every week!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fthisweekinreact.com%3Futm_source%3Ddev_crosspost" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fthisweekinreact.com%3Futm_source%3Ddev_crosspost" alt="banner"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


💸 Sponsor
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/nobodywho-ooo/nobodywho" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fthisweekinreact.com%2Femails%2Fissues%2F302%2Fnobodywho.png" alt="On-device AI for React &amp;amp; React Native"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/nobodywho-ooo/nobodywho" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;On-device AI for React &amp;amp; React Native&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;NobodyWho is a library for running LLMs locally &amp;amp; offline on any OS. GPU-accelerated via Vulkan or Metal.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Any LLM&lt;/strong&gt;: Gemma, Qwen, Mistral and more in .gguf format&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Type-safe tool calling&lt;/strong&gt;: automatically generates structured grammars from your function signatures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Multimodal input&lt;/strong&gt;: provide image and audio information to your LLM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Text-to-speech&lt;/strong&gt;: synthesize local WAV audio with Kokoro, Pocket TTS and Supertonic backends&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Speech-to-text&lt;/strong&gt;: transcribe audio into text with Whisper&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Voice Activity Detection&lt;/strong&gt;: know when to stop listening and start transcribing with Silero&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Available for &lt;strong&gt;React Native&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Expo&lt;/strong&gt;, but also for Flutter, Swift, Kotlin, Python, Godot and in React very soon thanks &lt;strong&gt;WebAssembly&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Star the&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://github.com/nobodywho-ooo/nobodywho" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;repo&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; if NobodyWho is useful to you, it is how people find us ❤️&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


⚛️ React
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;💸 &lt;a href="https://go.posthog.com/twir-oct21" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;build mode - What nobody tells you about writing agent skills&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🔐 &lt;a href="https://github.com/react/react/security/advisories/GHSA-xqc2-xf4c-x3h3" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React vulnerability - Unauthenticated Remote Code Execution in React Server Components&lt;/a&gt; - Patched in React 19.3.1 and the 19.0.9, 19.1.10 and 19.2.9 backports, together with a Server Functions DoS. In Next.js, the RCE affects &lt;code&gt;"use cache"&lt;/code&gt; functions returning multiple typed arrays. Upgrade to &lt;a href="https://nextjs.org/blog/nextjs-security-update-october-14-2026" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;16.4.1 or 15.5.28&lt;/a&gt;, which also fixes a critical RCE in sharp via SVG images.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📅 &lt;a href="https://luma.com/g9q690i2" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React Foundation Meetup - Nov 11, London&lt;/a&gt; - We &lt;a href="https://thisweekinreact.com/newsletter/300#react:~:text=React%20Foundation%20news" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;recently mentioned&lt;/a&gt; a React Foundation contributor summit, invite-only. But there’s also the first official React Foundation public meetup happening the same week at Meta King’s Cross.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;👀 &lt;a href="https://github.com/vercel/next.js/pull/99871" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Next.js PR - &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;Link prefetch="navigation"&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; - Adds a way to prefetch past the recently-introduced &lt;code&gt;await navigation()&lt;/code&gt; boundaries for links users are likely to click.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;👀 &lt;a href="https://react.dev/reference/dev-tools/react-devtools-cdt-mcp" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React docs - React DevTools for agents&lt;/a&gt; - The experimental &lt;code&gt;react-devtools-cdt-mcp&lt;/code&gt; package is now documented, with a live sandbox. Registers 12 additional React-specific tools with the Chrome DevTools MCP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📜 &lt;a href="https://nextjs.org/blog/improving-navigation-experience-in-v0-with-nextjs-16-4" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Improving navigation experience in v0 with Next.js 16.4&lt;/a&gt; - The &lt;code&gt;next-partial-prefetching-optimizer&lt;/code&gt; skill helps your agent refactor until an &lt;code&gt;instant()&lt;/code&gt; test proves the UI is ready before the click.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📜 &lt;a href="https://base-ui.com/blog/building-a-filterable-menu" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Building a filterable menu that works for everyone&lt;/a&gt; - Adding an input to a menu is easy, making it accessible isn’t. Base UI explains its ARIA choices (dialog, not combobox), keyboard and submenu UX.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📜 &lt;a href="https://mattrothenberg.com/notes/pure-ui-agentic-era/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Pure UI in the Agentic Era&lt;/a&gt; - Practical advice for reviewing agent-written UI: make components pure, pass state as explicit inputs, render every combination as a grid.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📦 &lt;a href="https://reactrouter.com/changelog#v850" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React Router 8.5 - Deprecated view transition APIs, unstable API-only mode&lt;/a&gt; - Now recommends React 19.3’s &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;ViewTransition&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, wrapped around an &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;Outlet&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;. The new API-only mode serves prerendered HTML from a CDN, while loaders and actions run on a server that can live on another origin.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📦 &lt;a href="https://github.com/pmndrs/react-three-fiber/releases/tag/v10.0.0-alpha.6" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React Three Fiber 10.0 alpha 6 - WebGPU renderer by default, better React 19 support&lt;/a&gt; - The upcoming major now works with &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;Activity&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;ViewTransition&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;. StrictMode and Fast Refresh no longer rebuild the Canvas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📦 &lt;a href="https://hydrogen.shopify.dev/update/hydrogen-2026-10-now-available" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Hydrogen 2026-10&lt;/a&gt; - Shopify Hydrogen is now a library, not a framework. Bring Shopify commerce to your existing Next.js or React Router app, with skills for coding agents. Built-in WebMCP support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📦 &lt;a href="https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/changelog/2026-10-ai-elements" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;shadcn/ui - AI Elements, Trace and Code Block&lt;/a&gt; - 21 copy-paste patterns for agent UIs. They replace Vercel’s AI SDK Elements, which will be deprecated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📦 &lt;a href="https://vinext.dev/blog" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Vinext 1.2 → 1.3 - 69% fewer JS requests per page, 5x faster cold starts, cache key collision fixes&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📦 &lt;a href="https://mutative.js.org/blog/releases/2.0" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Mutative 2.0 - Faster updates, safer patches&lt;/a&gt; - Same API, 3.6x faster than Immer on their benchmarks, for a bigger bundle (7.9 vs 3.6 kB).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📦 &lt;a href="https://github.com/immerjs/immer/releases/tag/v11.2.0" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Immer 11.2 - &lt;code&gt;isModified()&lt;/code&gt; helper&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📦 &lt;a href="https://github.com/bvaughn/react-window/releases/tag/2.4.0" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React Window 2.4 - Server rendering improvements&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📦 &lt;a href="https://astryx.atmeta.com/blog/introducing-astryx-richtext" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Astryx RichText - Lexical-based rich text field with lossless Markdown&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📦 &lt;a href="https://x.com/davidhaz/status/2110662315959803905" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React Bits 2.0 - 215 animated React components, rebuilt design tools&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📦 &lt;a href="https://c15t.com/changelog/3.0.0" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;c15t v3 - One consent engine for 8 frameworks, banner in the server HTML&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📦 &lt;a href="https://julesblom.com/react-trees" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React Trees Playground - Paste React code, see its parent and owner trees&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


💸 Sponsor
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://surveyjs.io/?utm_source=this-week-in-react&amp;amp;utm_medium=email" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fthisweekinreact.com%2Femails%2Fissues%2F293%2Fsurvey.jpg" alt="Make Forms a Scalable Part of Your React App"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://surveyjs.io/?utm_source=this-week-in-react&amp;amp;utm_medium=email" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Make Forms a Scalable Part of Your React App&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Product teams need to launch new forms and update existing ones. Developers shouldn't have to edit fields, labels, and validation rules for every change. &lt;a href="https://surveyjs.io/?utm_source=this-week-in-react&amp;amp;utm_medium=email" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SurveyJS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;strong&gt;provides a JSON-driven form library and an embeddable drag-and-drop form builder&lt;/strong&gt; for your React application.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Customize SurveyJS components to match your UI with custom themes or ready-to-use &lt;em&gt;theme adapters for Bootstrap, shadcn/ui, and Material UI&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;• Works with any backend and database&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
• Fits your existing design system&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
• Keeps developers in control of architecture and data&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Developers control the UI and data. Business users update forms visually without waiting for every change to be coded. 🚀&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


📱 React-Native
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fthisweekinreact.com%2Femails%2Fissues%2F302%2Freact-native-088.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fthisweekinreact.com%2Femails%2Fissues%2F302%2Freact-native-088.jpg" alt="React Native 0.88"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://reactnative.dev/blog/2026/10/19/react-native-0.88" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;React Native 0.88&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The new release is out with one of the largest runtime changes in years! Events are now dispatched through the W3C &lt;a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/EventTarget" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;code&gt;EventTarget&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; API by default. This is the same model as on the web, making it possible to share event handling code between web and native. This opens the path to web-compatible imperative APIs in the future. And yet, it’s a third release with no user-facing breaking changes, after 0.83 and 0.86.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Other key highlights include:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;SceneDelegate on iOS&lt;/strong&gt; - support for the &lt;code&gt;UIScene&lt;/code&gt; lifecycle required by the iOS 27 SDK, added additively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Variable fonts&lt;/strong&gt; - &lt;code&gt;fontVariationSettings&lt;/code&gt; on &lt;code&gt;Text&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;TextInput&lt;/code&gt;, on Android and iOS, in object or CSS string form.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;ArrayBuffer for Java TurboModules&lt;/strong&gt; - binary data no longer needs base64 or number-array encoding, and synchronous calls can borrow JavaScript memory instead of copying it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Swift Package Manager improvements&lt;/strong&gt; - still experimental, but iOS versions now come from the app's deployment target, and Xcode builds no longer break for libraries shipping their own &lt;code&gt;Package.swift&lt;/code&gt;. 0.89 targets SwiftPM as the default.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fthisweekinreact.com%2Femails%2Fissues%2F302%2Fexpo-sdk-58.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fthisweekinreact.com%2Femails%2Fissues%2F302%2Fexpo-sdk-58.jpg" alt="Expo SDK 58"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://expo.dev/changelog/sdk-58" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expo SDK 58&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A React Native release is not enough! Expo SDK 58 is out with React Native 0.88, built for iOS 27 and ready for iPhone Duo on day one, and it comes with a long list of improvements of its own. Too many to list them all, so here are the highlights:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Expo Modules 2.0 (beta)&lt;/strong&gt; - plain Swift and Kotlin classes with annotations, with sync calls 2.5-5.6x faster than the DSL on iOS and faster than TurboModules in all twelve Android microbenchmarks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Faster builds and faster modules&lt;/strong&gt; - prebuilt &lt;code&gt;expo-modules-core&lt;/code&gt; Android libraries cut a clean four-ABI debug build from about 80 seconds to about 39, and iOS calls passing long strings are up to 3.8x faster.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://expo.dev/blog/introducing-expo-app-intents" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;App Intents&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;strong&gt;(alpha)&lt;/strong&gt; - &lt;code&gt;expo-app-intents&lt;/code&gt; exposes your app to Siri, Shortcuts, Spotlight, and Apple Intelligence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Expo UI and Android home screen widgets&lt;/strong&gt; - lists recycle rows now, iOS gains NavigationStack and Toolbar, and &lt;code&gt;expo-widgets&lt;/code&gt; runs on Android with its own Hermes runtime.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;A CLI built for agents&lt;/strong&gt; - the experimental &lt;code&gt;@expo/agent-cli&lt;/code&gt; wraps Expo CLI, EAS CLI, and &lt;code&gt;expo-doctor&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Expo Router&lt;/strong&gt; - data loaders, SSR and middleware are now stable, alongside native tabs and a reworked navigation core.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;And a few more: an experimental Rust transformer for roughly 2x faster cold bundling, SwiftPM groundwork for Expo apps, and Expo Observe gaining control over automatic error recording.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;💸 &lt;a href="https://deploypulse.io/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;DeployPulse - Hosted OTA updates for React Native. A drop-in replacement for CodePush and EAS Update.&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;💬 &lt;a href="https://github.com/react-native-community/discussions-and-proposals/pull/1027" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;RFC - API removal strategy in React Native&lt;/a&gt; - Removed APIs like &lt;code&gt;InteractionManager&lt;/code&gt; throw on access. This proposes alternatives so that library authors can more easily use feature detection to keep supporting older React Native versions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📣 &lt;a href="https://github.com/zoontek/react-native-edge-to-edge" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React Native Edge to Edge is now deprecated&lt;/a&gt; - RN 0.86+ ships the fixes natively: set &lt;code&gt;edgeToEdgeEnabled=true&lt;/code&gt; in &lt;code&gt;gradle.properties&lt;/code&gt; instead.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📜 &lt;a href="https://x.com/reactnavigation/status/2110358651449868302" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Icons and iOS 27 updates in React Navigation 8&lt;/a&gt; - Native tabs now accept custom SF Symbols and VectorDrawables. With Nano Icons, you can use SVG icons in native tabs without hurting performance. Also includes filled Material Symbols and the iOS 27 prominent tab.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📜 &lt;a href="https://dev.to/amazonappdev/openiap-adds-supports-for-amazon-33b"&gt;OpenIAP adds support for Amazon&lt;/a&gt; - &lt;code&gt;react-native-iap&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;expo-iap&lt;/code&gt; can now sell on Fire OS and Vega OS with the same APIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📜 &lt;a href="https://expo.dev/blog/teamreach-ota-updates-relaunch" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Relaunching TeamReach: how OTA updates saved a 5,000,000-user cutover&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📜 &lt;a href="https://www.callstack.com/blog/multi-window-react-native-apps-with-the-meta-vr-layout-sdk" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Multi-Window React Native Apps With the Meta VR Layout SDK&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📜 &lt;a href="https://www.callstack.com/blog/give-qa-agents-the-controls-they-need-with-appduct" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Control App Test Conditions With Appduct for AI QA Agents&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;💸 &lt;a href="https://docs.maestro.dev/get-started/maestro-mcp?utm_source=this-week-in-react" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Maestro MCP - Let your coding agent write, run and debug your UI tests&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📦 &lt;a href="https://expo.dev/blog/xcode-27-device-hub-expo-device-hub" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;expo-device-hub - Your simulators and emulators in a browser tab&lt;/a&gt; - Also fixes the Expo CLI &lt;code&gt;i&lt;/code&gt; shortcut, broken by Xcode 27 after the removal of &lt;code&gt;Simulator.app&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📦 &lt;a href="https://github.com/DylanVann/react-native-fast-image/releases/tag/v10.0.0" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;FastImage 10.0 - New Architecture rewrite, &lt;code&gt;objectFit&lt;/code&gt; replaces &lt;code&gt;resizeMode&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;objectPosition&lt;/code&gt; added&lt;/a&gt; - The original library is actively maintained again.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📦 &lt;a href="https://swmansion.com/changelog/react-native-screens-4-30-0/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Screens 4.30 - iPhone Duo support, opaque headers fixed on iOS 26+, &lt;code&gt;prominentScreenKey&lt;/code&gt; for Tabs&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📦 &lt;a href="https://github.com/software-mansion/react-native-gesture-handler/releases/tag/v3.4.0" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Gesture Handler 3.4 - iOS SPM support, &lt;code&gt;immediatePressOut&lt;/code&gt; prop&lt;/a&gt;
