&lt;h2&gt;


🔀 Other
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📣 &lt;a href="https://web.dev/blog/crux-experimental-soft-navs/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Experimental soft navigation metrics now available in CrUX&lt;/a&gt; - Exciting news for SPA / client-side routing frameworks! Core Web Vitals takes into account soft navigations, measuring the full navigation session instead of only the initial page load, and the Chrome User Experience Report dataset now exposes these metrics as experimental. Use the &lt;a href="https://cruxvis.withgoogle.com/#/?view=cwvsummary&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Freact.dev%2F&amp;amp;identifier=origin&amp;amp;device=PHONE&amp;amp;periodStart=0&amp;amp;periodEnd=-1&amp;amp;display=p75s" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;CrUX Vis&lt;/a&gt; tool and check the “Include soft navigations” toggle to see the score impact on any site. The React site’s score is improving because subsequent navigations are faster than the initial page load.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🔐 &lt;a href="https://www.php.net/archive/2026.php#2026-10-21-5" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;PHP - Critical remote code execution vulnerabilities&lt;/a&gt; - These 2 “php2shell” RCEs look really bad: no login needed, affecting PHP since 5.4. Yes, that includes your WordPress and Laravel sites. Upgrade now!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📜 &lt;a href="https://www.joshwcomeau.com/css/interop-2027/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;The Future of CSS&lt;/a&gt; - Josh Comeau’s top 10 picks for Interop 2027, nicely presented with browser support and interactive demos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📜 &lt;a href="https://jakearchibald.com/2026/jpeg-xl-vs-avif/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;JPEG XL vs AVIF for web use-cases&lt;/a&gt; - JPEG XL recently landed in all browsers. AVIF remains better for lossy compression, but JPEG XL wins for lossless compression and recompressing existing JPEGs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📦 &lt;a href="https://devblogs.microsoft.com/typescript/announcing-typescript-7-1-beta/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;TypeScript 7.1 beta - New TypeScript API, Import Attributes in Ambient Modules, stable &lt;code&gt;es2026&lt;/code&gt; lib/target, performance improvements&lt;/a&gt; - The real highlight is the new TypeScript API, unlocking ecosystem tools such as TypeScript-ESLint to integrate with TypeScript 7. Content Mappers are a game changer for improving the type safety of external files such as MDX, Astro, CSS Modules, Vue, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📦 &lt;a href="https://blog.cloudflare.com/typescript-rust-port/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;tsrs - Rust port of the TypeScript 7 type checker and LSP&lt;/a&gt; - There have been a lot of TypeScript ports to Rust recently. The most promising one is already much faster than tsgo. It’s now supported by Cloudflare/VoidZero, incubating under the Oxc toolchain umbrella. Not a fork: they are actively collaborating with the TypeScript team and plan to keep it aligned with the reference implementation. The &lt;a href="https://building.owner.com/tsrs" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;backstory&lt;/a&gt; is also interesting, and shows the port will also speed up Oxlint type-aware linting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📦 &lt;a href="https://nodejs.org/en/blog/release/v24.22.0" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Node.js 24.22 LTS - &lt;code&gt;util.throttle()&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;util.debounce()&lt;/code&gt;, crypto improvements&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📦 &lt;a href="https://rsdoctor.rs/blog/release/release-note-2_0" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Rsdoctor 2.0 - Now Rspack-only, Agent CLI, 57% faster analysis, 56% smaller install, multi-compiler reports&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📦 &lt;a href="https://webpack.js.org/blog/2026-10-13-webpack-5-112/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Webpack 5.112 - SSR asset manifest, source map scopes, multi-entry library exports, async &lt;code&gt;DefinePlugin&lt;/code&gt; values&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📦 &lt;a href="https://astro.build/blog/astro-740/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Astro 7.4 - Build timings, separate build/runtime image services, parallel prerendering (experimental)&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




